 "text": "Hi, how have you been? A sketch is a short piece that plays straight through, often only one idea, while a study is longer and builds up several ideas. Not necessarily, a study can be performance too. It' just that studies usually last long enough to build up several ideas. You can use a tonal background paint first, and then paint the clouds on top. Which one comes first, the background or the clouds? Start painting the background, and once it dry, the clouds will still look soft and snowy. If you paint the clouds first, they can lose their texture. Fun idea. Which part are you stuck on? The basic shape, or the details?",
